Input: {"question": "Who directed the film \"Imitation of Life\"?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0279-f082b10a0d05:d00", "start": 0, "end": 97, "text": "Imitation of Life (1934 film) Imitation of Life is a 1934 American drama film directed by John M."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0279-f082b10a0d05:d00", "start": 98, "end": 104, "text": "Stahl."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0279-f082b10a0d05:d00", "start": 105, "end": 296, "text": "The screenplay by William Hurlbut, based on Fannie Hurst's 1933 novel of the same name, was augmented by eight additional uncredited writers, including Preston Sturges and Finley Peter Dunne."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0279-f082b10a0d05:d00", "start": 297, "end": 415, "text": "The film stars Claudette Colbert, Warren William and Rochelle Hudson and features Louise Beavers and Fredi Washington."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0279-f082b10a0d05:d00", "start": 416, "end": 521, "text": "The film was originally released by Universal Pictures on November 26, 1934, and later re-issued in 1936."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0279-f082b10a0d05:d00", "start": 522, "end": 585, "text": "A 1959 remake with the same title was directed by Douglas Sirk."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0279-f082b10a0d05:d00", "start": 586, "end": 618, "text": "In 2005, \"Imitation of Life\" was"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0279-f082b10a0d05:d01", "start": 0, "end": 177, "text": "Imitation of Life (1959 film) Imitation of Life is a 1959 American romantic drama film directed by Douglas Sirk, produced by Ross Hunter and released by Universal International."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0279-f082b10a0d05:d01", "start": 178, "end": 261, "text": "It was Sirk's final Hollywood film and dealt with issues of race, class and gender."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0279-f082b10a0d05:d01", "start": 262, "end": 384, "text": "\"Imitation of Life\" is the second film adaptation of Fannie Hurst's novel of the same name; the first, directed by John M."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0279-f082b10a0d05:d01", "start": 385, "end": 413, "text": "Stahl, was released in 1934."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0279-f082b10a0d05:d01", "start": 414, "end": 572, "text": "The film's top-billed stars are Lana Turner and John Gavin, and the cast also features Sandra Dee, Dan O'Herlihy, Susan Kohner, Robert Alda and Juanita Moore."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0279-f082b10a0d05:d01", "start": 573, "end": 598, "text": "Kohner and Moore received"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0279-f082b10a0d05:d02", "start": 0, "end": 96, "text": "the film has a score of 87 out of 100 based on 16 critics , indicating `` universal acclaim '' ."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0279-f082b10a0d05:d02", "start": 97, "end": 224, "text": "[ 17 ] In 2015 , BBC Online ranked the film as the 37th greatest American movie ever made , based on a survey of film critics ."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0279-f082b10a0d05:d02", "start": 225, "end": 292, "text": "[ 18 ] Awards and nominations More information Award , Category ..."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0279-f082b10a0d05:d02", "start": 293, "end": 334, "text": "Award Category Nominee ( s ) Result Ref ."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0279-f082b10a0d05:d02", "start": 335, "end": 544, "text": "Academy Awards Best Supporting Actress Susan Kohner Nominated [ 19 ] Juanita Moore Nominated Directors Guild of America Awards Outstanding Directorial Achievement in Motion Pictures Douglas Sirk Nominated [ 20"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0279-f082b10a0d05:d03", "start": 0, "end": 36, "text": "Stahl : Adaptations and Remakes '